## Context

Coverage today is 100% shell integration — there are no `*_test.go`
files. Several pieces of `tickets/tools/go/` have subtle behavior
that shell tests cannot reach efficiently or precisely:

- `parseHeaderLine` (`ticket.go:73`) — whitespace-before-colon
  handling, non-letter starts, embedded `_`/`-`.
- `parseErg` state machine (`ticket.go:111`) — CRLF endings, no
  trailing newline, magic line padded with whitespace, repeated
  `Blocked-by` headers, separators inside the body section.
- `parseLogTimestamp` (`archive.go:14`) — length-edge cases (`<16`),
  missing space delimiter, both fallback formats.
- `detectCycles` (`validate.go:111`) — self-loop (`A` blocked by
  `A`), 3-node cycle, multiple disjoint cycles, branched DAG with
  no cycle.
- `jsonEscape` (`ticket.go:214`) — control chars, embedded backslash
  sequences.

## Actions

1. Add `tickets/tools/go/ticket_test.go` covering `parseHeaderLine`,
   `parseErg`, `jsonEscape`. Use table-driven tests.
2. Add `tickets/tools/go/validate_test.go` covering `validateErg`
   (one case per rule) and `detectCycles`.
3. ~~Add `tickets/tools/go/archive_test.go` covering
   `parseLogTimestamp`.~~ DROPPED: `parseLogTimestamp` does not exist
   in the codebase (`archive.go` was never added). No coverage gap.
4. Keep tests pure — no filesystem fixtures except via `t.TempDir()`.
5. Naming: `TestParseErg_CRLF`, `TestDetectCycles_SelfLoop`, etc.

Depends on 0024 only because that ticket establishes the test layout
convention; can run in parallel if we agree on a layout up front.

## Test

- `go test ./tickets/tools/go/...` passes locally.
- `go test -cover` reports per-file coverage; target ≥80% for
  `ticket.go` and `validate.go`.

## Exit criteria

- Two `*_test.go` files committed (`ticket_test.go`, `validate_test.go`).
  Action 3 (`archive_test.go`) was dropped — `parseLogTimestamp` does not
  exist in the codebase.
- Local `go test ./...` green.
- Coverage report attached in PR description.
